# GenomicVariantTeam rules — `Genomic_Variant_umbrella`

A **Genomic_Variant** is a set of changes in the tested sample relative to a reference
sequence for a genome (the mCODE genomic-variant profile). This section is an object with
`count_of_Genomic_Variants`, `llm_confidence_score`, and `Genomic_Variants` — **one object
per distinct variant** the report reports (point mutation, indel, fusion, CNV-as-variant,
or an explicit "Not Detected" call for a specifically tested locus).

## 1. What belongs here (vs other_molecular_biomarker)

- **HERE (Genomic_Variant):** gene sequence changes — `JAK2 V617F`, `BRAF V600E`,
  `EGFR exon 19 deletion`, fusions, CNVs reported as variants — anything with HGVS-style
  change detail (c./p./g.), a VAF, a clinical significance call, or a genomic position.
- **NOT here (→ other_molecular_biomarker_umbrella):** protein-expression by IHC
  (ER, PR, HER2, Ki-67, PD-L1) and aggregate molecular scores (TMB, MSI, LOH, HRD,
  ctDNA Tumor Fraction). Those have no per-variant change detail.
- **NOT here:** histological findings, general lab markers, testing METHODS as names.

## 2. One object per distinct variant

- One `Genomic_Variants[]` entry per distinct variant. The same variant restated in two
  places is still ONE object — do not duplicate. Two different variants in the same gene
  are two objects.
- `count_of_Genomic_Variants` MUST equal the length of `Genomic_Variants`.

## 3. Per-variant fields — EVERY field emitted, `null` when absent

Emit ALL fields on every object; use JSON `null` (never `"N/A"`/`""`/`"None"`) when the
value is not on the page. Never infer a value the document does not state.

- `gene_studied` — the gene examined. Call `hgnc_normalize` for the HGNC-preferred symbol;
  keep the printed surface if it differs and the dictionary can't justify a rewrite
  (then set `needs_review: true` with a `review_reason`).
- `method` — VERBATIM (NGS, PCR, FISH, Sanger sequencing, ...).
- `result` — VERBATIM call (Detected, Not Detected, Positive, Negative).
- `variant_allele_frequency` — VAF VERBATIM with units (e.g. `"20.3%"`).
- `dna_change_type`, `amino_acid_change_type` — codified type as printed (open vocab:
  Wild type / Deletion / Duplication / Insertion / Deletion-Insertion / Inversion /
  Substitution / Frameshift / Initiating Methionine / ...). VERBATIM; `null` if not stated.
- `genomic_dna_change` (`g.`), `coding_dna_change` (`c.`), `amino_acid_change` (`p.`) —
  **VERBATIM exactly as printed**, including when the report omits the `g.`/`c.`/`p.`
  prefix (e.g. `1849G>T`, `V617F`). Do NOT add a prefix the document omits.
- `genomic_reference_sequence` (NC_/LRG), `transcript_reference_sequence` (NM_ — preserve
  the version integer, `NM_004333.4` ≠ `.3`), `amino_acid_reference_sequence` (NP_).
- `clinical_significance` — VERBATIM (Pathogenic / Likely Pathogenic / VUS / Likely Benign /
  Benign, or the narrative as printed).
- `genomic_source_class` (Somatic / Germline / Likely Somatic / Unknown),
  `human_reference_sequence_assembly_version` (`hg19 (GRCh37)`, `GRCh38`),
  `allelic_state` (Heterozygous / Homozygous), `chromosome_identifier` (`chr7`),
  `genomic_position`, `exon` — all VERBATIM, `null` when not on the page.
- `page_number` (DERIVED) — a SINGLE integer (e.g. `1`), the page where the variant is
  found. NEVER a list — `page_number: [1]` is wrong; emit `page_number: 1`. (The plural
  `page_numbers` list belongs to the tested-biomarker umbrella, not here.)

## 3b. Canonical HGVS — separate from the verbatim fields

For **every variant** that has any populated `*_change` field (`coding_dna_change`,
`amino_acid_change`, `genomic_dna_change`), you **MUST** call `hgvs_validate` on the
printed change and emit a `hgvs_normalized` object (`{coding, amino_acid, genomic, valid,
version, backend}`) on the variant record. This is REQUIRED — downstream verifiers trust
the agent's `hgvs_normalized.valid` flag and skip a redundant byte-level re-check when
it's present; omitting it forces a re-validation that can mis-flag values containing
invisible OCR characters (unicode minus, NBSP, en-dash). `hgvs_normalized` is INTERNAL
(dropped at production) and is SEPARATE from the verbatim fields so the printed surface is
preserved AND the canonical form is available. On tool failure leave the fields null but
STILL emit `hgvs_normalized: {valid: false}` — never omit the object.

**Tool budget — converge fast.** Call `hgnc_normalize` AT MOST ONCE per gene and
`hgvs_validate` AT MOST ONCE per change notation. Do NOT re-call a tool with the same
argument or loop on it. Once you have the gene key and the validated change for each
variant, STOP calling tools and emit the Final Answer JSON immediately — a single
clean `Genomic_Variant_umbrella` object. A `null` from a tool is a final answer for that
field, not a reason to retry.

## 4. Concatenation + provenance

- When a single field's value is spread across non-adjacent fragments, concatenate them
  with **` | `** (space-pipe-space).
- Emit a `provenance` ARRAY on each variant. There MUST be **one entry per populated
  field** of the variant record (every field whose value is not null). Each entry is
  `{field_name, block_id, page, type, rationale}`:
  - `type` ∈ `verbatim | inferred | derived | absent`.
  - `block_id` cites the source block (use only block_ids returned by your tools).
  - `rationale` is **REQUIRED for every entry, including `verbatim`**. It is a short
    natural-language clause naming the source location and what made you confident in
    the value. **Never** put the literal word `"verbatim"`, `"inferred"`, `"derived"`,
    or the type tag itself in the `rationale` slot — that field is for prose, not the
    type label. **Never** leave `rationale` as `null` for a populated field.

  Good rationales (verbatim case):
    `"matches the 'Gene' column of the variant table at block_10, page 1"`
    `"the literal string 'V617F' in the protein-change column of block_10"`
    `"taken from the 'Method' field of the variant summary on page 2"`

  Bad rationales (do NOT emit):
    `"verbatim"`     ← that's the TYPE tag, not a rationale
    `null`           ← rationale is required, even for verbatim fields
    `"copied from the report"` ← too vague; name the source location

## 5. OCR / inference flag

Dictionary first. If `hgnc_normalize` resolves the gene exactly, use it silently; if it's a
fuzzy/context correction or the surface is OCR-garbled, set `needs_review: true` with a
`review_reason` (independently verified downstream). Never silently rewrite a token the
dictionary couldn't justify; the verbatim surface stays in the verbatim fields.

---

Now run the ReAct loop and produce the `Genomic_Variant_umbrella` object — one object per
distinct variant, each with all fields (null when absent) + its `provenance`.
